## Prompt

Create ONE square grayscale polar-UV cloud texture concept on pure black, using the attached screenshot as the ONLY reference for BOTH COMPOSITION AND CLOUD SHAPES, not just style. Reconstruct the visible clouds without the advertisement, lettering, house, terrain, characters, QR or logos.
Reference fidelity: the right half contains a huge continuous cloud bank, tall broad uneven towers at far right, a saddle then another tall flat-topped irregular tower toward middle. Its broad gray shadow occupies most of the lower body, with a few wide interlocking pale light planes on its crown and an irregular shelf-shaped shadow boundary, NOT lots of round highlighted bubbles. Left side is mostly empty sky above a low thin extended distant bank with just a few small uneven rising crowns and long horizontal trailing shelves. Closely echo those silhouettes, relative sizes and shadow silhouettes. Use subdued flat animation-background paint, 3 or 4 broad connected tonal planes with slight soft blending, no detailed realistic cauliflower, no repeating brush stamps.
Translate this asymmetric panorama arrangement into a polar UV atlas: UV center represents zenith, circumference horizon; reference's huge right-hand bank occupies primarily RIGHT outer sector from about 1 to 5 o'clock and reaches inward more deeply; its bright crown points LEFT toward center. Reference's small low left horizon bank becomes a narrow shallow irregular band mainly in LEFT outer sector, barely extending inward, with wide black empty sky inside it. A sparse low continuation may occupy bottom edge; top-left and center remain largely black. Do NOT make a donut, horseshoe, symmetrical wreath, giant left crescent, separate diagonal cigar-shaped hero or uniformly spaced satellite clouds. The large right bank must visually dominate as in the reference.
All crown silhouettes and center-directed illumination obey radial UV: inward faces are clear, softly rounded but precise; outward undersides have very narrow gentle fading and readable broad forms. Flat shadow silhouettes must remain clearly readable. Brightness is a filled plane, no white strokes, halos, doubled contours, embossing, scalloped internal rims, fine noise or distorted streaks. Keep black margin at image border. Grayscale only, black empty sky. No labels or diagrams. This is cloud shading artwork, not a binary alpha mask.
